.Dd August 12, 2026
.Dt INCA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm inca
.Nd pointer-first infinite canvas compositor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Op Fl s Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Wayland compositor based on wlroots. It places windows on a continuous
canvas that can be panned and zoomed instead
of using a traditional tiling layout.
.Pp
Window placement, input, effects, monitor rules, and bindings are configured at
runtime with Lua.
Valid file changes are reloaded automatically; an invalid
change leaves the last valid configuration active.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar path
Load the Lua configuration at
.Ar path .
.It Fl d
Enable debug logging from wlroots.
.It Fl s Ar command
Run
.Ar command
through
.Pa /bin/sh
when the compositor starts.
The process group receives
.Dv SIGTERM
when Inca! exits.
.It Fl v
Print the name and version, then exit.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The first readable configuration is used in this order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
The path passed with
.Fl c .
.It
.Ev INCA_CONFIG .
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/inca/config.lua .
.It
The installed
.Pa share/inca/config.lua .
.It
.Pa ./config/config.lua .
.It
.Pa $HOME/.config/inca/config.lua .
.El
.Pp
The shipped configuration documents every available setting.
Default controls
include:
.Bl -tag -width "Super-Button3" -compact
.It Alt-Tab
Focus and center the next window.
Add Shift to move backward.
.It Super-c
Center the active window.
.It Super-0
Reset canvas pan and zoom.
.It Super-minus , Super-equal
Zoom out or in.
.It Super-m
Collapse or restore the active window in place.
.It Super-Shift-c
Close the active window.
.It Super-f
Toggle fullscreen.
.It Super-Shift-less , Super-Shift-greater
Move the active window to the monitor on the left or right.
.It Super-Button1
Move a window.
.It Super-Button2
Pan the canvas.
.It Super-Button3
Resize a window.
.El
.Pp
Dragging empty canvas or scrolling with two fingers pans it.
Pinch gestures zoom the canvas.
Nearby window edges snap together, and holding a dragged window at
an output edge pans the viewport.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width INCA_CONFIG
.It Ev INCA_CONFIG
Path to the runtime Lua configuration.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default per-user configuration path.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory used to create the Wayland socket.
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Name of the Wayland display created by Inca!.
.It Ev WLR_*
Backend and renderer settings understood by wlroots.
.El
